---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import BrowseSidebar from "../../components/BrowseSidebar.astro";
import { GITHUB_GAME_DATA } from "../../data/github-game-data.js";
const source = `https://github.com/openfrontio/OpenFrontIO/blob/${GITHUB_GAME_DATA.revision}/src/core/configuration/Config.ts`;
---
<Layout title="Early Game Guide — OpenFront Wiki" description="A practical OpenFront early-game guide to spawning, capacity, first structures, scouting, and the first safe attack."><SiteHeader /><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[230px_minmax(0,1fr)]"><aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-20 lg:h-[calc(100vh-6rem)] lg:overflow-y-auto" data-pagefind-ignore><details open><summary class="mb-3 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-glow lg:cursor-default">Browse Pages <span class="lg:hidden">▾</span></summary><BrowseSidebar /></details></aside><main class="min-w-0"><nav class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-dawn/50" data-pagefind-ignore><a href="/" class="hover:text-aquarius">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/category/getting-started" class="hover:text-aquarius">Getting Started</a><span>/</span><span class="text-dawn">Early game</span></nav><header class="border-b border-white/10 pb-8"><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-glow">Player guide</p><h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-wide text-white sm:text-4xl">Early game</h1><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-dawn/80">Build enough capacity to grow, enough economy to act, and enough reserve to survive the first border test.</p></header><article class="wiki-content mt-8" data-pagefind-body><div class="guide-callout"><strong>Your first objective is not maximum expansion.</strong><p>It is a stable position: room below troop capacity, one useful production path, and a border you can defend while your army approaches the 35–50% recovery band.</p></div><h2>First minutes</h2><ol><li>Spawn where expansion has multiple safe directions and you are not immediately boxed into a single front.</li><li>Claim connected territory before reaching for isolated edges or exposed water.</li><li>Build a City when the capacity increase will support continued growth; completed City levels add a large capacity bonus in the current code.</li><li>Choose Factory, Port, or defensive infrastructure based on the map route you can actually protect.</li></ol><h2>Pick the first fight</h2><p>Use a controlled attack rather than emptying the army. Compare the neighbor's troop density and likely reserve with your own capacity percentage. A weakly held border is a better first target than a dense position behind a Defense Post, even if the latter looks closer.</p><h2>Common early mistakes</h2><ul><li>Building several expensive systems before establishing a safe economy.</li><li>Attacking from a nearly full army and then losing the ability to recover after the push.</li><li>Taking territory that creates a new exposed border without enough reserve.</li><li>Treating raw troop count as more important than troops-per-tile and capacity percentage.</li></ul><h2>Continue here</h2><p><a href="/guides/attacking-effectively">Attacking effectively</a>, <a href="/guides/defense-and-recovery">Defense & recovery</a>, <a href="/guides/economy-and-logistics">Economy & logistics</a>, and <a href="/Game_Settings">Game Settings</a>.</p><p class="source-note">Capacity, attack order, and starting-manpower context checked against <a href={source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFrontIO Config.ts ↗</a>.</p></article></main></div><SiteFooter /></Layout>